--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -4,6 +4,13 @@ Newest first. O&G Workbench combines Geo Workbench (well data manager, with Cros
 
 ## O&G Workbench (Geo + Petro + Seismic)
 
+### Integrated v0.9.70 — Seismic Map drawings stability: layout that settles, no hang after Finish, panels and windows that clean up after themselves
+
+- **No hang after a fault polygon's Finish (TK-AUD-001).** The Map drawings panel's hints wrapped to their own width, and with the panel's natural size and its scroll bar that could keep asking for another layout pass; the project tree's rebuild after a polygon's Finish then waited on Tk's idle work, which never ran out - the polygon was saved, but the panel flashed and Seismic stopped responding. The hints now wrap to the width the panel shows, a scroll bar that would only come and go is held shown, and the tree's scroll position is restored by one callback when Tk is next idle instead of waiting there. The workflow is unchanged: open Map drawings, edit a polygon's vertices, Finish - it saves, the panel stays open, the map and tree refresh.
+- **A closed Map drawings panel lets go (TK-AUD-002).** Each panel bound Enter, Esc, Delete and Backspace on the Seismic window and never unbound them: every panel ever opened kept answering those keys and kept its tab, map and figure alive. Each panel now keeps its own bindings and removes only those, however it closes (its X, its map, the project or Seismic closed, the map's window destroyed first, or while a polygon is being edited - the edit is cancelled, nothing saved). Fifty opens and closes leave the Seismic window's bindings as they were.
+- **Nothing left waiting for a closed window (TK-AUD-003).** Closing a project now cancels each map's waiting redraws and closes its Map drawings panel before the windows go, as closing a map does; a scroll frame's waiting layout pass is cancelled when it is destroyed; the application's own waiting callbacks (the tree's scroll, the well filter) and the close-request watch go with its window. A closed project's map is let go (its figure with it).
+- **Variable traces go with their owners (TK-AUD-004).** Seismic's Find well box and Cross Section's property fields left their variable traces behind, holding destroyed windows - and their Tk interpreters - alive. Their traces are now removed when the window goes.
+
 ### Integrated v0.9.69 — Audit corrections: stale Seismic deletes, atomic horizon delete, typed Undo, appended shapefiles, native-axis statistics, zone collisions, nested transactions
 
 - **A Seismic deletion deletes only what it deleted (AUD-001).** A horizon or fault is now deleted by the object this window loaded - its project identity, its stored row and its picks - never by its name. A window that deleted H could, on its next save, delete a new H another window (or program) had made and saved since; now that save is refused as a conflict (Reload keeps the newer H; Overwrite deletes it only by your explicit choice), and **Delete** in the tree refuses an object changed, replaced or made again elsewhere since it was loaded ("was not deleted ... Nothing was changed"). Applies to horizons and faults.
